course: dictionary
lesson: 9856
title: Symbolically: standing for an idea
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Symbolically means in a way that uses a symbol to stand for an idea, rather than in a real or practical way. A symbol is something that stands for something bigger, like a dove standing for peace.
explain: «Some Christians read some miracle stories symbolically.» The word "read" is your context clue. You read a story for its meaning, so here symbolically means the story stands for a deeper idea, not only for something that happened in a practical way.
explain: Symbolically also appears in maths. «x + 3 = 7» uses letters and signs instead of words, so it is written symbolically. Ask yourself: is this real and practical, or does it stand for an idea? If it stands for an idea, the word is symbolically.
fact: Symbolically means in a way that uses a symbol to stand for an idea.
fact: «Symbolically» comes from «symbol», and it tells you how something is done or shown.
fact: In baptism, the water symbolically washes away sin, which means it stands for cleansing rather than only washing the body.
fact: In maths, a word problem can be written symbolically, like «x + 3 = 7».
fact: A good check: swap in "in a real, practical way". If the sentence still makes sense, the meaning fits a real act; if not, the word is probably symbolically.
exercise: «Some Christians read some miracle stories symbolically.» What does symbolically mean here? | Loudly | Very quickly | In a real, practical way | *As a symbol that stands for a deeper idea
exercise: In maths, «x + 3 = 7» is written symbolically. What does that mean? | It is a story about a king | It uses only words | *It uses letters and signs instead of words | It is written in very big writing
exercise: «The flag was symbolically important to the team.» What does symbolically important suggest? | Important for one minute | Important because it is heavy | *Important because it stands for an idea | Important only to the cook
test: «Christians share bread and wine symbolically to remember Jesus.» What does symbolically tell you? | *The bread and wine stand for something more than food and drink | The bread and wine are sold in a shop | The bread and wine are thrown away | The bread and wine are eaten only for lunch
test: Which one is written symbolically? | A story about a dragon | *x + 3 = 7 | Seven apples and three pears | Three plus seven is the answer
exam: «A storm in the poem may symbolically show a character's anger.» What does this mean? | The storm is real, and the character is standing in it | *The storm stands for the anger, as a symbol | The character is cold and wet | The poem is only about the weather
